  We created a set of obfuscated scientific papers in which a logical
  structure is changed to a visual one, and trained several models to
  reconstruct the original papers.  The results were not very good for
  out-of-the-box open source \acro{LLM}s, but improved after fine
  tuning.  The results for the \acro{BERT} model were also acceptable.
  The trained models were able to convert the initially
  visually formatted articles from arXiv to logical formatting, but
  the quality of the translation needs improvement.  We argue that
  reconstruction of the logical structure requires several reading
  passes with changing focus.
